gcm/live draw: exclusive [perf-x] counters for the method loop, the ld_flush split and program identity (RSX_PERF_X=1).

Pass 119 (frame-rate ideas review): counters only, no behaviour change. Active only
with RSX_PERF=1, RSX_PERF_X=1 and inside the RSX_PERF_PROF=A,B window; none nested in another 2125 timer.
- Method loop (cellGcmSys.c, the per-word path every command takes while live draw is on, gcm_word_diag() = 1):
  one command in 32 is timed word by word: the whole loop, the time inside rsx_live_draw_method and inside the
  final dispatch (gcm_3d/2d_method, flip, user command; "2d" = the part outside gcm_3d_method). Scaled to all
  commands of the period, minus the timer cost a calibration at the window start measures ("bias", printed once as
  "[perf-x] calibration"): loop, live, disp, excl = loop - live - disp (io2ea per word, the diagnostic tests, the SET_OBJECT bookkeeping).
- ld_flush split (rsx_live_draw.c, both the frames-in-flight and the single path): fence wait, info-queue drain,
  retired-texture release, allocator reset, list reset; per second in [perf-x] and per frame (frame = present
  flush) at the window end: "[perf-x-flush] frames=N ms/frame mean/p99/max".
- Program identity in ld_pso: FP memo compare, FP size scan (END bit search), VP memo compare, VP FNV, FP key hash
  (structural or FNV), rsx_fp_collect_constants: calls, bytes, ms and memo hits.
Line "[perf-x] t=..." per second with the other [perf-*] lines.
Diagnostic LD_TEX_WATCH=2 (pool mode, for the patch 2082 question): every 1024th presented frame write-protect the
local range LD_TEX_WATCH_RANGE=LO,HI (hex local offsets, default 0x0FF00000,0x10000000) and log the first store into
each 4 KB page ([tex-watch], up to 4096 lines; committed read-write pages only), whether or not the bitmap
missed it. The handler now passes on a fault it cannot resolve (a page it did not protect: before, a store into a
not yet committed page looped in the handler). LD_TEX_WATCH=1 is otherwise unchanged.
